From 6eba14131fdac6219f2188f7f196874fe99e93cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: boyfromcave <boyfromcave@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:03:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] chainparams: regtest keeps Equihash (48,5) under every
 network upgrade

v4.5.0's CChainParams::EquihashN/K returned consensus.nEquihashN/K on
regtest before consulting the per-upgrade table. 6.20.0's
GetEquihashOverride() walks NetworkUpgradeInfo on every network, so
activating the Ycash upgrade (374d694f) on regtest switches the solver to
(192,7): about five minutes per generated block on an Apple M-series
machine. Because Blossom, Heartwood and Canopy must activate after Ycash,
any regtest that needs them becomes impractical.

The consumers that matter, the miner / generate path (miner.cpp) and the
height-aware solution-size check in ContextualCheckBlockHeader (main.cpp),
both read CChainParams::EquihashN/K, and the context-free
CheckEquihashSolution already accepts a (48,5) solution, so a regtest
guard in the two accessors keeps mining and validation consistent.
Mainnet and testnet are untouched.

Verified on regtest: Overwinter, Sapling, Ycash, Blossom, Heartwood and
Canopy active at height 1 (tip branch id 19bd2d2f), 110 blocks in under
a second, then shield, Sapling->Sapling, deshield and a transparent send
all mined.
---
 src/chainparams.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/chainparams.cpp b/src/chainparams.cpp
index 75c9f7fae..970fb71e2 100644
--- a/src/chainparams.cpp
+++ b/src/chainparams.cpp
@@ -981,6 +981,8 @@ const NUInfo* GetEquihashOverride(int nHeight, const Consensus::Params& params)
 } // namespace
 
 unsigned int CChainParams::EquihashN(int nHeight) const {
+    if (NetworkIDString() == CBaseChainParams::REGTEST)  // regtest keeps (48,5) under every upgrade, as in v4.5.0
+        return consensus.nEquihashN;
     if (auto info = GetEquihashOverride(nHeight, consensus)) {
         return info->nEquihashN;
     }
@@ -988,6 +990,8 @@ unsigned int CChainParams::EquihashN(int nHeight) const {
 }
 
 unsigned int CChainParams::EquihashK(int nHeight) const {
+    if (NetworkIDString() == CBaseChainParams::REGTEST)  // regtest keeps (48,5) under every upgrade, as in v4.5.0
+        return consensus.nEquihashK;
     if (auto info = GetEquihashOverride(nHeight, consensus)) {
         return info->nEquihashK;
     }
